{
  "name": "VeeR EL2 TMR"
  "testpoints": [
    {
      "name": "baseline",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that the design is capable of completing workloads from `software test suite` (STS)
        * Provide golden test results for comparison against tests with fault injection enabled

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2
        * Do not inject any faults

        Check:
        * Verify the correctness of test software execution
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.1",
      "tests": [
        "baseline_workload_1",
        "baseline_workload_2",
        "baseline_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["baseline"]
    },
    {
      "name": "fault_detection",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of detecting injected faults in the design

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Use SV test scenario with bit flip injection using force-release mechanism
        * Inject bit flip into a signal covered by TMR logic
        * Constrain the bit flip injection time with the state of the core rather than hardcoded time delay
        * Execute basic test software on VeeR EL2

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.2",
      "tests": [
        "fault_detection_scenario_1",
        "fault_detection_scenario_2",
        "fault_detection_scenario_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["fault_detection"]
    },
    {
      "name": "recovery_success",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of recovering from detected Fault Event

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Use SV test scenario with bit flip injection using force-release mechanism
        * Inject bit flip into a signal covered by TMR logic that triggers Fault Event Detection in the design that should be recoverable
        * Constrain the bit flip injection time with the state of the core rather than hardcoded time delay
        * Execute basic test software on VeeR EL2

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic performs succesfull recovery from Fault Event
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Success Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "recovery_success_scenario_1",
        "recovery_success_scenario_2",
        "recovery_success_scenario_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["recovery_success"]
    },
    {
      "name": "recovery_failure",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Verify TMR logic behaviour upon detecting Fault Event that puts the design into unrecoverable state

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Use SV test scenario with bit flip injection using force-release mechanism
        * Inject bit flip into a signal covered by TMR logic that triggers Fault Event Detection in the design that should be unrecoverable
        * Constrain the bit flip injection time with the state of the core rather than hardcoded time delay
        * Execute basic test software on VeeR EL2

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic detects unrecoverable failure
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Failed Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "recovery_failure_scenario_1",
        "recovery_failure_scenario_2",
        "recovery_failure_scenario_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["recovery_failure"]
    },
    {
      "name": "critical_failure",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Verify design behaviour upon Fault Event that is not detected by TMR logic and cause critical failure of the design

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Use SV test scenario with bit flip injection using force-release mechanism
        * Inject bit flip into a signal that is not detected by TMR logic and that triggers a critical failure of the design
        * Constrain the bit flip injection time with the state of the core rather than hardcoded time delay
        * Execute basic test software on VeeR EL2

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic does not detect injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if design reached a critical failure
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "critical_failure_scenario_1",
        "critical_failure_scenario_2",
        "critical_failure_scenario_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["critical_failure"]
    },
    {
      "name": "fuzz",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of detecting injected faults in the design
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of recovering from detected Fault Event
        * Find and record fault injection strategies that lead to TMR failures:
          * Fault Events that are detected by TMR logic and that put the design into unrecoverable state
          * Fault Events that are not detected by TMR logic and cause critical failure
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`
        * Record `Time To Recovery Failure`
        * Record `Time to Critical Failure`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Generate fault injection scenario (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` using one of available fault generation models
        * Randomize seed value for generating fault injection strategy
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection
        * Store `Time To Recovery Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Fault Event Detection that triggers Recovery Failure
        * Store `Time To Critical Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Critical Failure
        * Store FIS if the simulation ended with one of the following:
          * Detected Fault Event and Design Recovery Failure
          * Undetected Fault Event and Desgin Critical Failure
        * Repeat test procedure for multiple generated FIS and for all workloads from STS

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic performs succesfull recovery from Fault Event
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Success Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
        * Verify if TMR logic performs recovery from Fault Event but fails
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Failed Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
        * Verify if design reached a critical failure
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
            * Must not be detected
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "fuzz_workload_1",
        "fuzz_workload_2",
        "fuzz_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["fuzz"]
    },
    {
      "name": "fuzz_directed",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of detecting injected faults in the design
        * Prove that TMR logic is capable of recovering from detected Fault Event
        * Find and record fault injection strategies that lead to TMR failures:
          * Fault Events that are detected by TMR logic and that put the design into unrecoverable state
          * Fault Events that are not detected by TMR logic and cause critical failure
        * Verify the behaviour on specified area of the design
        * Record `Time To Fault Event Detection`
        * Record `Time To Recovery Failure`
        * Record `Time to Critical Failure`

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Constrain the list of 'upsetable' signals only to considered design area
        * Generate fault injection scenario (FIS) with `faultergeist-gen` for each considered area and using one of available fault generation models
        * Randomize seed value for generating fault injection strategy
        * Enable fault injection for VeeR EL2 based on generated FIS
        * Execute test software from STS on VeeR EL2
        * Store `Time To Fault Event Detection` records as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and first Fault Event Detection
          * Record time between every successful Fault Event Recovery and subsequent Fault Event Detection
        * Store `Time To Recovery Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Fault Event Detection that triggers Recovery Failure
        * Store `Time To Critical Failure` as one of the test results
          * Record time between start of the fault injection process and Critical Failure
        * Store FIS if the simulation ended with one of the following:
          * Detected Fault Event and Design Recovery Failure
          * Undetected Fault Event and Desgin Critical Failure
        * Repeat test procedure for multiple generated FIS, for all workloads from STS and for all considered design areas

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic performs succesfull recovery from Fault Event
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Success Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
        * Verify if TMR logic performs recovery from Fault Event but fails
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Failed Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
        * Verify if design reached a critical failure
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
            * Must not be detected
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.3",
      "tests": [
        "fuzz_directed_area_1_workload_1",
        "fuzz_directed_area_2_workload_1",
        "fuzz_directed_area_M_workload_1",
        "fuzz_directed_area_1_workload_2",
        "fuzz_directed_area_2_workload_2",
        "fuzz_directed_area_M_workload_2",
        "fuzz_directed_area_1_workload_N",
        "fuzz_directed_area_2_workload_N",
        "fuzz_directed_area_M_workload_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["fuzz_directed"]
    },
    {
      "name": "mtbf_measurement",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Gather from fuzz tests:
          * `Time To Fault Event Detection`
          * `Time To Recovery Failure`
          * `Time To Critical Failure`
        * Aggregate results into Mean Time Between Failures grouped by:
          * Severity:
            * Fault Detection
            * Recovery Failure
            * Critical Failure
          * Area of fault injection
        * Gather:
          * Total Number of injected faults
          * Total Number of detected fault events
          * Total Number of successfull recoveries
          * Total Number of failed recoveries
          * Total Number of critical failures
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.4",
      "tests": [
        "gather_mtbf_measurements"
      ]
      "tags": ["mtbf_measurement"]
    },
    {
      "name": "regression",
      "desc": '''
        Intent:
        * Prove that TMR logic works as expected and no bugs are introduced
        * Prove that TMR logic will no longer enter incorrect state after injecting faults that were previously known to cause a failure after the underlying bug was fixed

        Stimulus:
        * Configure VeeR EL2 with TMR feature enabled
        * Use SV test scenario with bit flip injection using force-release mechanism
        * Inject bit flips into signals from general group that was known to trigger unwanted Recovery Failure or Critical Failure
        * Constrain the bit flip injection time with the state of the core rather than hardcoded time delay
        * Execute on VeeR EL2 the same test software that was running in the simulation when the bug was discovered

        Check:
        * Verify if TMR logic detects injected faults
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Detection Notification
        * Verify if TMR logic performs succesfull recovery from Fault Event
          * Check TMR output port responsible for Fault Event Recovery Success Notification
          * Compare simulation results against golden results from `baseline` tests
      '''
      "stage": "DV0.2",
      "tests": [
        "regression_scenario_1",
        "regression_scenario_2",
        "regression_scenario_N",
      ]
      "tags": ["regression"]
    }
  ]
}
